.TH EZ-SSH 1 "2026-11-26" "ez-ssh 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ez-ssh \- local, zero-cloud SSH & SFTP manager TUI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ez-ssh
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ez-ssh
is a fast, zero-cloud SSH and SFTP Terminal User Interface (TUI) written in Go.
It manages SSH hosts, AES-256-GCM encrypted credentials, SSH keypairs,
local/remote/SOCKS5 port forwarding tunnels, reusable command snippets,
\fIknown_hosts\fR entries, connection audit logs, dual-pane SFTP transfers, and
embedded terminal tabs from a single static binary.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the startup banner with the installed version and exit.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.B Alt+1 / Alt+2
Switch to the Vaults or Dual-Pane SFTP workspace.
.TP
.B Alt+3 .. Alt+9
Switch between active embedded SSH session tabs.
.TP
.B Alt+Left / Alt+Right
Cycle across open workspace tabs.
.TP
.B Ctrl+W
Close the active SSH session tab.
.TP
.B 1 .. 6 / Tab
Switch Vault modules (Hosts, Keychain, Port Fwd, Snippets, Known Host, Logs).
.TP
.B /
Fuzzy search within the active view.
.TP
.B i
Toggle the detail inspector panel.
.TP
.B q / Ctrl+C
Quit \fBez-ssh\fR (when outside a connected SSH PTY session).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ez-ssh/.vault.key
Master encryption key (mode 0600) used to seal stored passwords and passphrases.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ez-ssh/vault.db
Local SQLite database (mode 0600) storing hosts, keychain items, tunnels, snippets, and audit logs.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ez-ssh/logs/
Optional recorded SSH session transcripts (mode 0700).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EZ_SSH_CONFIG_DIR
Overrides the default configuration directory (\fI~/.config/ez-ssh\fR).
